<b>Good work today.</b>

19:56.780 --> 19:57.780
<b>Good work.</b>

20:01.350 --> 20:03.320
<b>You have
1 new message.</b>

20:09.690 --> 20:11.560
<b>So that girl’s on the move, huh?</b>

20:21.570 --> 20:23.010
<b>Yes, hello?</b>

20:23.010 --> 20:26.910
<b>Ah. Makabe-kun?
I just got your message.</b>

20:26.910 --> 20:28.250
<b>What’s happened since then?</b>

20:29.450 --> 20:33.980
<b>Tanigawa-san’s definitely headed there.</b>

20:33.990 --> 20:36.350
<b>To the giant material evil?</b>

20:36.350 --> 20:37.690
<b>Yes.</b>

20:37.690 --> 20:41.190
<b>And I’m just about to meet up with Kobayakawa-kun.</b>

20:41.660 --> 20:43.390
<b>I’ll also head over now.</b>

20:43.400 --> 20:44.730
<b>Where are you right now?</b>

20:44.730 --> 20:47.400
<b>I’m near the train station in Sakuragi Town.</b>

20:47.400 --> 20:50.070
<b>Could you meet me in front of the station in an hour?</b>

20:50.070 --> 20:51.200
<b>Gotcha.</b>

20:52.240 --> 20:53.870
<b>Better hurry up!</b>

20:55.370 --> 20:58.340
<b>This is where Bun-chan...?</b>

20:58.340 --> 20:59.680
<b>Yeah.</b>

20:59.680 --> 21:01.350
<b>Is something here?</b>

21:01.950 --> 21:05.580
<b>I just feel... like I was called here.</b>

21:09.590 --> 21:11.090
<b>Why is someone else here?</b>

21:15.930 --> 21:18.900
<b>Could he be the guy from that night?</b>

21:18.900 --> 21:20.360
<b>Yeah.</b>

21:20.370 --> 21:21.670
<b>You wanna leave now?</b>

21:22.900 --> 21:24.170
<b>Definitely not.</b>

21:41.220 --> 21:44.020
<b>For now, let me do the talking.</b>

21:49.190 --> 21:50.330
<b>Hey, you.</b>

21:50.330 --> 21:51.700
<b>What are you doing here?</b>

21:55.300 --> 21:56.000
<b>Hey!</b>

21:56.000 --> 21:57.400
<b>You came.</b>

21:59.810 --> 22:00.870
<b>I was waiting for you.</b>

22:01.870 --> 22:02.910
<b>Excuse me?</b>

22:05.710 --> 22:08.880
<b>I knew you’d come,
so I was able to wait here for you.</b>

22:08.880 --> 22:12.050
<b>But I was really anxious.</b>

22:12.750 --> 22:15.150
<b>Thank you for coming.</b>

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
words that no one else knew.

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Ah, I thought that being alone

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
Sore de ii to omotta

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

24:19.980 --> 24:22.940
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

24:20.550 --> 24:22.580
<b>I put on a cute ribbon!</b>

24:22.580 --> 24:25.450
<b>Taruto-chan, that hole-patterned ribbon is cute.</b>

24:25.450 --> 24:28.650
<b>This isn’t hole-patterned!
It’s polka dotted!</b>

24:28.650 --> 24:30.090
<b>Huh? Those aren’t holes?</b>

24:30.090 --> 24:31.890
<b>Obviously not!</b>

24:31.890 --> 24:33.160
<b>What’s this problem with holes?</b>

24:33.160 --> 24:34.430
<b>Roku’s saying this is full of holes.</b>

24:34.430 --> 24:36.390
<b>Oh, so you like holes, Roku?</b>

24:36.390 --> 24:39.400
<b>If you’re talking about liking them, it’s only
the polka dotted, hole-patterned ones.</b>

24:39.400 --> 24:43.900
<b>[Note: In Japanese, “ana” can either mean “hole” or be short for “announcer.”]</b>

24:39.400 --> 24:41.500
<b>When you say “ana,”
I think of “announcer.”</b>

24:41.500 --> 24:43.900
<b>In other words, Sukawara Akira,
and people like her.</b>

24:43.900 --> 24:46.170
<b>No, when you say “ana,”
you think of polka dots.</b>

24:46.170 --> 24:47.170
<b>Announcers!</b>

24:47.170 --> 24:47.840
<b>Polka dots.</b>

24:47.840 --> 24:48.510
<b>Announcers.</b>

24:48.510 --> 24:48.970
<b>Polka dots.</b>

24:48.970 --> 24:49.510
<b>Announcers.</b>

24:49.510 --> 24:50.010
<b>Polka dots.</b>

24:50.010 --> 24:50.440
<b>Announcers.</b>

24:50.440 --> 24:50.840
<b>Polka dots.</b>

24:50.840 --> 24:53.740
<b>Next time: The World’s Membrane is Full of Holes.</b>

24:53.750 --> 24:55.510
<b>Huh? What’s the matter, Taruto-chan?</b>

24:55.010 --> 24:59.950
<b>The World’</b>s Membrane is Full of Holes

24:55.510 --> 24:57.520
<b>I feel like I’m about to get an ulcer...</b>
